# ── Build artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# data/clean/ is regenerated by notebook 01 on every run. Committing it would mean
# the repo can contain a parquet file that disagrees with the notebook that claims
# to produce it — which is the exact class of failure this project is about.
data/clean/
*.parquet

# ── Jupyter ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*/.ipynb_checkpoints/*
.jupyter/
.virtual_documents/

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.Python
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Secrets / credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing in this project currently needs credentials. These patterns are here so
# that if a data-source API is ever added, the keys cannot be committed by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
credentials/
secrets/
service-account*.json

# ── OS / editor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ── Notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# data/raw/ is deliberately NOT ignored — the analysis is not reproducible without
# it and the files are small (~1 MB total). If the source datasets' licences do not
# permit redistribution, ignore data/raw/ here and document the download steps in
# the README instead.
#
# output/ is deliberately NOT ignored — the CSVs there are project deliverables
# (baselines, aggregates, the crosswalk) and are meant to be inspectable on GitHub
# without running anything.
